This crate (`symphonia-codec-g7231`) is a pure-Rust G.723.1 decoder. It is licensed under the
Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

It is a bit-exact fixed-point port of the FFmpeg G.723.1 decoder: `libavcodec/g723_1dec.c`,
`libavcodec/g723_1.c` and `libavcodec/g723_1.h`, together with the helpers they use from
`libavcodec/celp_math.c`, `libavcodec/celp_filters.c`, `libavcodec/acelp_vectors.c` and
`libavutil/common.h`. The LSP, gain, combinatorial and pitch tables (`src/tables.rs`) were
extracted programmatically from those files. The algorithm is defined by ITU-T Recommendation
G.723.1 ("Dual rate speech coder for multimedia communications transmitting at 5.3 and 6.3
kbit/s") and its Annex A (silence compression); FFmpeg's implementation reproduces the Recommendation's
tables and fixed-point arithmetic.

